In a message dated 9/26/2006 4:22:04 AM Central Standard Time, 
ecartis@digitalkingdom.org writes:


> 
> How don't cats describe themselves?  "I am hungry"
> 

Cats don't describe anything; they have no way to describe anything.  People 
may attribute what a cat does as making a statement, but such statements are 
more like simple commands: "I want out; open the door!", "Pet me!", "Feed me!"  
These aren't descriptions.  Behavior (and reactions in general) are not 
descriptions.  

stevo
           
